                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>- </run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>Look-alike Exclusion Filter</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>: There is a group of subscribers who did not order prior to their subscriptions. The way we assigned them a look-alike person might affect the results. Thus we added a filter to exclude them.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>&#9;- </run>
                <run fontsize='9' italic='true'>Subscribers who didn&apos;t order prior to Subs</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>: We assign them a user who had their first order on the same day. Since the look-alike is picked randomly due to missing historical data; this might create a low, long-term look-alike group performance.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>&#9;-  </run>
                <run fontsize='9' italic='true'>Subscribers who never ordered: </run>
                <run fontsize='9'>We assign them a user who created an account but never ordered (a.k.a. prospect user). Since they will never order but Subscribers will keep paying us; this will result in pure incrementality on profitability, and thus a bias in our results.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>Abbreviations:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>- LaL: </run>
                <run fontsize='9'>Look-alike group. Alternatively, they might be called </run>
                <run fontsize='9' italic='true'>Control group.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>- Subs Revenue: </run>
                <run fontsize='9'>Subscription Fee Revenue.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>Assumptions:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>- We have a data mismatch around 10% with local data on subscription counts. We assume that this doesn&apos;t create a bias in our results.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>- We can&apos;t find look-alikes for 2% of our subscription cohorts. We assume that this also doesn&apos;t create a bias in our results.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>- All costs and revenues mentioned in the legend for </run>
                <run fontsize='9' italic='true'>Drivers of (Un)Profitability</run>
                <run fontsize='9'> charts are </run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>per order</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>Blockers:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='9'>- We currently can&apos;t replicate this study to PY or TB entities due to bad data quality in central tables.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='pane'>
                <format attr='minheight' value='-1' />
                <format attr='maxheight' value='-1' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
