        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Square' />
            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>Subscription Types:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>- Free Trial: </run>
                <run fontsize='9'>If the customer is subscribed to their first subscription without paying any fee.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>- Heavy Discount: </run>
                <run fontsize='9'>If the customer is subscribed to their first subscription with a discount above 50%. The data collection on Heavy-Discount users are semi-automatised now. We have used the latest prices in this document ( https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Nu3r2c99-fY2uDSbb0fxAEfrrfUmEi3kRZ_HVg-tZ8w/edit#gid=658478430 ), to calculate which users would have 50% discount. Next step would be connecting each entities&apos; user-based automated campaign data.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>- Other: </run>
                <run fontsize='9'>The rest of the subscribers. Assuming full data quality, this group would be called &quot;Organic&quot; or &quot;Subscribers without Flash Sales&quot;.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='pane'>
                <format attr='minheight' value='-1' />
                <format attr='maxheight' value='-1' />
                <format attr='minwidth' value='-1' />
                <format attr='maxwidth' value='-1' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
